      "subject": "feat(executive): talk to the Chief Agent and decide its proposals in the Executive Office (EW-1)",
      "body": "Wires the first Executive Office sections to Runtime, using only endpoints that already exist. The conversation sends the owner's question as an executive event; the Chief Agent reasons over governed knowledge and its answer becomes a proposed decision with an approval addressed to the owner, so nothing it says takes effect without the owner (ADR-0041, propose only). The Approval Center approves or rejects those decisions (a rejection needs a reason) and lists canonical promotions waiting for review with a way into Canonical Review. The command deck reads activation, autonomy, learning cycles, pending approvals and the canonical count, and Learn now runs a real learning cycle. Reads are fast records polled every 30 s; the slow education projections are deliberately not used here. Unwired parts keep their design-preview badge and mixed sections say Partly live. The approved look is locked by a new Executive Office UI contract (same fingerprint method as Knowledge Operations, separate script so it cannot touch the certified KO contract), and npm run build now verifies both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
